{ github.com/mathiasvatter/cksp-compiler/issues/61: a <declare> that borrows the name of a
  <define> arrives at the parser as <declare 1: int>. The <define> is written correctly, so
  the report belongs on the declaration - and it has to name what the source says, not the
  value it was substituted for. }

on init
    define some_define := 1
    declare <|borrowed_name|>some_define : int := 43
end on
